# Keep LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites checked-out
# files to CRLF. That would break this suite in ways that look like real
# failures: tests/test_web_assets.py compares the assembled document against the
# files on disk, tests/test_pricing_parity.py parses the JS pricing table out of
# it with anchored regexes, and tests/test_dashboard_js.py concatenates the JS
# parts and runs them under node. All of them compare text, and none of them
# should have to care which platform checked it out.
#
# It also keeps the delivered bytes identical across platforms, which matters
# because the dashboard is assembled from these files at import and served as
# one document.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png binary
*.svg text eol=lf
